  "question": {
    "text": "In reaction $\\mathrm{A}+2 \\mathrm{~B} \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{C}+\\mathrm{D}$, initial concentration of $\\mathrm{B}$ was $1.5$ times of $\\mathrm{[A]}$, but at equilibrium the concentrations of $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{B}$ became equal. The equilibrium constant for the reaction is :",
